Z||000000||Child Of Rod||07-01-2000||12:17 PM||||Well I got my 86 SE running yesterday...and I noticed something...<BR>Whenever I press the gas it takes the tranny a little while to engage, and the tires rip the pavement apart when it does.<BR>When the tranny is switching gears you can watch the rpms goes up real high for a 2-4 seconds then it will engage, again ripping up the pavement.  That one is the worst..it does it while moving.<BR>I know it may be impressive to do in front of the ricers around me, but something is wrong.  My 84 doesn't do this, neither does my friend's Formula.<BR>After I fix this I guess I will have to apply for the title  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">)<BR>Thanks in advance.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Bruce||07-01-2000||03:28 PM||||Make sure that there is sufficient, and correct, tran. fluid.||||reg||1
